ticket: {'identifier': 'KS-1275', 'title': 'Published POST /lifecycle-events description still enumerates an old verb list (originate.openapi.ts:1847-1861 -> secuura-api.yaml)', 'state': 'Backlog', 'priority': 'Medium', 'description': '# KS-1275 ORDER-1 PIN THE DECLARED ORDER OF LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS (the order z.enum publishes and the 400 message joins) — Wednesday\'s task for Ornith, TEST_ONLY, **ONE existing test file, one hunk, one cell added, no product file** (written 16:19 on 2026-09-20, round 22)\n\nFile: `Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/__tests__/lifecycleEventRepo.test.ts`\nTip: `e470198783bcb1ef0eac94780f87579974051423`\nRunner: `jest`\n\nWritten from develop `e470198783bcb1ef0eac94780f87579974051423` (`git -C "/Volumes/DevMASTER/!CODING/Secuura/Blockchain/2_Project_Files" log -1 e47019878`, read-only; the tip of the #1097-#1099 merge, 2026-09-20 05:54:10 +1000). The test file at that tip is **169 lines**, read whole; its full content is in `files[...]` of your input. The product the cell pins is `Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/lifecycleActions.ts` (**66 lines**, read whole), the `LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS` array at `:38-63`. This service runs **JEST**.\n\n## THE MODE — read this twice\n\n**TEST_ONLY.** Your diff touches EXACTLY ONE file: the test file above, MODIFIED IN PLACE (`--- a/<path>` / `+++ b/<path>`, the path exactly as written above). You never touch `lifecycleActions.ts` or any other product file: the behaviour is already right at the tip, and this cell PINS it.\n\n## What the cell pins (one paragraph)\n\n`lifecycleActions.ts` is the single source of truth for the `/lifecycle-events` verb set, and it is consumed in THREE published places: `originate.openapi.ts:1740` and `:1765` register `z.enum(LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS)`, whose array order is generated verbatim into `docs/openapi/secuura-api.yaml`; `routes/documents.ts:2416` builds the 400 body\'s `Accepted: ${LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS.join(\', \')}` from the same order; `docs/VOCABULARY.md` mirrors it. The suite\'s existing vocabulary pin (`lifecycleEventRepo.test.ts:50-73`) asserts `[...LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS].sort()` against a sorted literal, so it pins MEMBERSHIP and is **order-blind by construction**: any permutation of the sixteen verbs leaves it green while the published enum and the 400 message both change. Nothing else in the repo asserts the order — `grep -l LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS` at the tip returns exactly one test file (this one). This change adds ONE cell that joins the declared array and compares it to the declared order as a single string. Every existing cell is unchanged. **It pins TODAY\'s declaration order and decides nothing about KS-1275\'s own fix** (replacing the hand-written verb list in the `POST /lifecycle-events` description at `originate.openapi.ts:1847-1861` with a pointer to the enum, plus a spec regeneration): that is a two-file change and is NOT this task.\n\n## The exact change — ONE hunk in the test file\n\nThe new cell goes at the end of the `describe(\'LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS vocabulary pin\', ...)` block opened at `:49`, directly above that block\'s closing line `});` (`:82`, the ONE trailing context line). There is NO leading context: the line above (`:81`, `  });`) stays and is not written. Copy every line byte for byte. Every `+` line is ASCII only. There is no blank line anywhere in the fence. Keep the header exactly as shown. **Your diff MUST begin with the two file-header lines, above the `@@` line: `--- a/Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/__tests__/lifecycleEventRepo.test.ts` then `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/__tests__/lifecycleEventRepo.test.ts`.**\n\n```\n@@ -82,1 +82,5 @@\n+  it(\'RED KS-1275 ORDER-1: LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS is declared in ONE order, the order z.enum publishes and the 400 message joins\', () => {\n+    const declaredOrder = [...LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS].join(\',\');\n+    expect(declaredOrder).toEqual(\'rights-unassign,share-revoke,share-permission-change,rename,delete,restore,share-recipient-change,share-expiry-change,share-token-rotate,share-resend,share-attach-consent,protect,unprotect,note,certified,verified\');\n+  });\n });\n```\n\n`LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS` is already imported by the file at `:41` (`import { LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS } from \'../lifecycleActions\';`) — you add NO import. The cell needs no mock: it reads a frozen `as const` array, so the `jest.mock(\'../db\')` / `jest.mock(\'../utils/logger\')` doubles at `:20-34` and the `beforeEach` at `:45-47` are irrelevant to it and are not touched. The expected string is the sixteen verbs in declaration order, taken from `lifecycleActions.ts:39-62` in file order (`:50-54` and `:57-59` are comment lines inside the array and contribute no verb).\n\n## Cells\n\n- `declaredorder` = `RED KS-1275 ORDER-1: LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS is declared in ONE order, the order z.enum publishes and the 400 message joins`\n\n## Red cells\n\nThe cell below is a GENUINE assertion-red: it fails under each tamper and passes at the tip. It is declared here rather than with a 🔴 in its title because every `+` line in this diff must be ASCII only.\n\n- RED KS-1275 ORDER-1: LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS is declared in ONE order, the order z.enum publishes and the 400 message joins\n\n## Tampers\n\nBoth are BLOCK tampers (two whole consecutive lines each) inside the `LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS` array literal opened at `lifecycleActions.ts:38` (`export const LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS = [`) and closed at `:63` (`] as const;`). Each swaps two adjacent entries, so the SET is unchanged and only the ORDER moves — which is exactly what the existing sorted pin cannot see. Each `From` block occurs EXACTLY ONCE in `lifecycleActions.ts` at the tip (whole lines, byte for byte, verified); `Line:` is the cross-check.\n\n### SWAPNOTECERT — the KS-1172 pair is declared in the other order\nFile: `Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/lifecycleActions.ts`\nLine: 60\nFrom:\n```\n  \'note\',\n  \'certified\',\n```\nTo:\n```\n  \'certified\',\n  \'note\',\n```\nReds: `declaredorder`\n\n### SWAPFIRSTTWO — the first two KS-387 verbs are declared in the other order\nFile: `Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/lifecycleActions.ts`\nLine: 39\nFrom:\n```\n  \'rights-unassign\',\n  \'share-revoke\',\n```\nTo:\n```\n  \'share-revoke\',\n  \'rights-unassign\',\n```\nReds: `declaredorder`\n\n## Controls\n\n- `accepts exactly the no-dedicated-endpoint verbs`\n- `inserts and returns the stored record shape`\n- `maps a NULL subquery resolution to LIFECYCLE_TARGET_NOT_FOUND`\n\n*(The file\'s fourth vocabulary cell, the KS-1172 / KS-1173 `toContain` cell at `:75-81`, is ALSO green under both tampers — `toContain` is order-blind too — but its description begins with a non-ASCII character, so it is not declared as a control here; the builder matches controls as literal prefixes.)*\n\n## THE CELLS — state it to yourself before you write a line\n\nAt the untouched tip the new cell passes: `[...LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS].join(\',\')` is the sixteen verbs in the order they are written at `lifecycleActions.ts:39-62`, which is the string the cell asserts. Under SWAPNOTECERT the joined string ends `...,unprotect,certified,note,verified` instead of `...,unprotect,note,certified,verified`, so the cell fails by assertion. Under SWAPFIRSTTWO it begins `share-revoke,rights-unassign,...`, the same failure at the other end. Under BOTH, every existing cell stays green: the `:50` pin sorts both sides, the `:75` cell uses `toContain` / `not.toContain`, and the repository cells only ever pass the single verb `\'rights-unassign\'` as a value (`:91`), whose membership neither tamper touches.\n\n## Premises (measured — by reading the tip, NOT by running anything)\n\n- **Premise: each `From` block is unique.** Whole-line consecutive match over `lifecycleActions.ts` at the tip: `  \'note\',` + `  \'certified\',` starts at exactly one line, **60**; `  \'rights-unassign\',` + `  \'share-revoke\',` at exactly one line, **39**. Each of the four lines also occurs exactly once on its own (`grep -c -Fx` = 1 for each).\n- **Premise: the anchor.** `:82` is `});` (column 0), closing the `describe` opened at `:49`; `:81` is `  });` and `:83` is blank, so the trailing context line is non-blank and the insertion is pure (no blank line is asked of you anywhere). The same text `});` also sits at `:47`, `:123`, `:131` and `:169`, so the hunk header\'s line number is what places it.\n- **Premise: no `+` line re-adds a tip line.** `declaredOrder`, `KS-1275`, `ORDER-1` and `.join(\',\')` occur **0** times in the test file at the tip. The only `+` line that also occurs at the tip is the closing `  });` (unavoidable for a new cell).\n- **Premise: nothing else in the repo pins this order.** `git grep -l LIFECYCLE_EVENT_ACTIONS` at the tip: `docs/VOCABULARY.md`, `anchoring/src/anchorSchema.ts` (a COMMENT only, `:40`), `anchoring/src/anchoring.openapi.ts`, `originate/src/originate.openapi.ts`, `originate/src/routes/documents.ts`, `originate/src/lifecycleActions.ts`, and this one test file. `grep -i \'Accepted:\'` over `originate/src/__tests__` returns **0** — no cell asserts the 400 message text, so no other cell can red under a reorder. The only other originate test naming a verb is `ks466-documents-malformed-id-guard.test.ts:182`, which sends `action: \'rights-unassign\'` as a VALUE (membership, not order).\n- **No backslash** in any `+` line (0, counted). **No non-ASCII** in any `+` line (0, counted).\n- **Premise: the runner.** `originate/package.json` at the tip has `"test": "jest"` and `jest` / `ts-jest` in devDependencies, and no vitest — the builder auto-detects jest; the `Runner:` line above agrees with it.\n\n## NOT MEASURED — state this in the READY\n\n**No suite was run for this brief and no scratch clone was made.** The writing seat was barred from running any test suite and from touching any local port (a live PostgreSQL of unknown ownership sits on 127.0.0.1:5432), so unlike the round-19 briefs this one carries **no** tip-suite count, **no** per-tamper red count and **no** checker pre-run. Everything above is read from the blobs at `e47019878`. **Before this is queued, run the real checker on the brief\'s own diff in a `--shared` scratch clone at the tip** — the expected result is the originate suite green at the tip with one extra cell, and each tamper reding exactly `declaredorder` and nothing else.\n\n## Output\n\nExactly ONE ```diff block, nothing outside it: `--- a/Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/__tests__/lifecycleEventRepo.test.ts` / `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/__tests__/lifecycleEventRepo.test.ts`, then the hunk above exactly as shown (`@@ -82,1 +82,5 @@`).\n\n## Notes for the raise (not for the model)\n\n- Test-only, zero product bytes. **Raise tier: TIER 2. Refs KS-1275** (and KS-1172 / KS-1173, whose three verbs are the last three of the pinned order). **NEVER Closes** — KS-1275\'s own defect (the stale hand-written verb list in the published description, `originate.openapi.ts:1847-1861`, plus the `npm run generate-openapi` regeneration) is untouched here and stays Backlog.\n- **Not from a gate.** Round 20 (2026-09-20 15:28-15:35) rejected KS-1275 for the local model as "multi-file by its own fix shape" — correct for the TICKET\'S FIX, which this brief does not attempt. This is a completeness pin of the vocabulary module the ticket\'s fix will point its prose AT, in the N97-1 / N99-1 species: a shape the suite provably cannot see today.\n- **Collision: none.** No held `READY_*` carries a hunk in `lifecycleEventRepo.test.ts`; the only READY that ever did is `READY_KS-1172-A3_…_2026-09-15`, whose content is AT the tip (the three verbs and the `:75` cell), i.e. a spent hold. `lifecycleActions.ts` is not touched by this diff at all.\n- The other stale-prose sites KS-1275 names (`documents.ts:2384-2387`, `lifecycleEventRepo.ts:7`) are COMMENT-tier work and are deliberately NOT in this brief; `documents.ts` additionally holds the KS-1277 comment_patch READY of round 21.\n\n## Build line (not for the model)\n\n```\nbash tasks/test_only/build_test_only_input.sh KS-1275 night/inputs/test_only_1275ORDER-1.json night/briefs/KS-1275.md ctx=65536\n```\n'}
