ticket: {'identifier': 'KS-1272', 'title': 'api-gateway boot: the platform-DB de-dup DELETE fails 22P02 on every boot where platform_document_registry.tenant_id is uuid — "Platform DB migrations INCOMPLETE — 1 FAILED"', 'state': 'Backlog', 'priority': 'Low', 'description': '# KS-1272 — Wednesday\'s task for Ornith, VITEST, **CODE_PATCH MODE: ONE changed line in `startup-migrations.ts` + ONE NEW test file** (written 21:58 on 2026-09-20 from the file at develop `dc061f2bb6dff9180a0724b1d1d5c50b9a0173fa` — `startup-migrations.ts` read whole, 1227 lines)\n\nWritten from origin develop `dc061f2bb6dff9180a0724b1d1d5c50b9a0173fa` (read by `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/develop` at 21:52 AEST 2026-09-20; the #1101 KS-1282 N99-1 merge).\n`Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/startup-migrations.ts` read WHOLE at that tip: blob `ed3e52142`, **1227 lines** (`wc -l`), 57,305 B.\nThe reference test `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1062-startup-migrations-tenant-summary-first-error.test.ts` (blob `0ec64a16e`, 111 lines) was read whole. The ticket KS-1272 (Backlog, Low, 0 attachments, 0 comments, related KS-598) was read.\n\n## THE MODE — read this twice\n\n**CODE_PATCH.** This service runs **VITEST** (`vi`, not `jest`). Your diff contains EXACTLY TWO files:\n1. `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/startup-migrations.ts` — ONE hunk, ONE changed line (line 1077).\n2. `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1272-platform-dedup-uuid-tenant-id.test.ts` — ONE NEW file, written out for you below.\n**Nothing else.** Not the ks1062 reference test, not any other test, not `docker/init-platform/01-platform-schema.sql`. Write the paths exactly as `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/...` — the same form as `product_file` and `suggested_test_file` in your input.\n\n## What is wrong (one paragraph)\n\nEvery api-gateway boot on kintsugi logs `Migration FAILED on platform {"error":"invalid input syntax for type uuid: \\"\\""}` and then `Platform DB migrations INCOMPLETE — 1 FAILED {"applied":6,"failed":1}`. The `platformMigrations` list (`:1060-:1093`, seven statements, run by `migrateDatabase(pg, platformDbUrl, \'platform\', platformMigrations)` at `:1094`) carries the KS-39 #4 de-dup `DELETE FROM platform_document_registry a USING platform_document_registry b ...` at `:1075-:1077`, whose last line compares `COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\') = COALESCE(b.tenant_id, \'\')`. On `secuura_platform` the column `platform_document_registry.tenant_id` is `uuid` (the init script `docker/init-platform/01-platform-schema.sql:209-213` runs first on a fresh database, so the in-code `CREATE TABLE ... tenant_id TEXT` at `:1063-:1070` is a no-op there), and Postgres cannot cast `\'\'` to uuid: `SELECT COALESCE(NULL::uuid, \'\')` is `ERROR 22P02 invalid input syntax for type uuid: ""`. The statement fails on every boot, so the platform summary is permanently `INCOMPLETE — 1 FAILED`, which hides the next real platform-migration failure — the signal KS-950 made visible. **This task (the ticket\'s own Recommendation):** make the platform de-dup type-agnostic with `a.tenant_id IS NOT DISTINCT FROM b.tenant_id` (valid for TEXT and for UUID, and NULL = NULL as before), plus one new vitest file whose 🔴 cell runs the platform list against a fake uuid-typed platform database.\n\n**NOT in this task — line `:473` stays exactly as it is.** The MAIN database\'s `CORE_MIGRATIONS` list carries the same de-dup at `:471-:473` with the same `COALESCE` line (5-space indent there; 11-space indent at `:1077`). On the main database the column is TEXT, and `COALESCE(x, \'\') = COALESCE(y, \'\')` treats a NULL tenant_id and an empty-string tenant_id as EQUAL, whereas `IS NOT DISTINCT FROM` does not — changing `:473` would change which rows that DELETE removes: a data-affecting semantic change the ticket does not ask for (Refs KS-1272; line 473 deliberately untouched, reason: the main column is TEXT and the two forms differ on NULL vs \'\'). The second control cell below pins that exactly one `CORE_MIGRATIONS` statement still carries `COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\')` — a diff that also edits `:473` goes RED there. Also not in this task: the ticket\'s "decide which declaration is canonical" question, the init SQL, and the `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX` at `:1078`.\n\n## WHY THE TEST CALLS THE CODE DIRECTLY\n\nNo database is reachable in the checker. `runStartupMigrations()` is called DIRECTLY with `pg` redirected, ONLY for the product file, to a fake Pool — the idiom of the existing `ks1062-startup-migrations-tenant-summary-first-error.test.ts` (`Module._resolveFilename` intercepts the product\'s bare `require(\'pg\')` at `:945`; `vi.mock` cannot reach a bare require). The fake does no I/O. For the database named `qa_platform_uuid` it behaves like a platform database whose `tenant_id` is uuid: any statement containing `COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\')` throws `invalid input syntax for type uuid: ""`, everything else succeeds. For `qa_platform_index` it refuses ONE other platform statement (the `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS uq_pdr_hash_tenant`) with a message that is not "already exists", so the summary counts it — that is the control which proves ONE refused platform statement is exactly what the platform summary reports as `{applied: 6, failed: 1}`. The main database `qa_main` is never refused.\n\n## Where (every bold site MUST change; the (correct) ones stay)\n\n- `:1074` — (correct) `        // UNIQUE index the verification.ts ON CONFLICT clause errors.` — the first context line of your hunk. Stays.\n- `:1075` — (correct) ``        `DELETE FROM platform_document_registry a USING platform_document_registry b`` — the platform de-dup opens. Stays.\n- `:1076` — (correct) `         WHERE a.id > b.id AND a.content_hash = b.content_hash` — stays. (This text also occurs at `:472` in the MAIN list with a 5-space indent; yours is the 11-space one directly under `:1075`.)\n- `:1077` — **must change** ``           AND COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\') = COALESCE(b.tenant_id, \'\')`,`` — the ONE line you replace (11 leading spaces; the line ends with a backtick and a comma that close the SQL template string — keep them). The same text with a 5-space indent sits at `:473` in `CORE_MIGRATIONS` and STAYS.\n- `:1078` — (correct) ``        `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS uq_pdr_hash_tenant ON platform_document_registry(content_hash, tenant_id)`,`` — trailing context. Stays. (Also at `:474` with a 2-space indent; yours is the 8-space one.)\n\nLine 473 (the MAIN list\'s de-dup, `     AND COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\') = COALESCE(b.tenant_id, \'\')` followed by the closing backtick and comma, 5-space indent) STAYS and is deliberately NOT a bullet above: its text is byte-identical to `:1077` once indentation is stripped, and a `## Where` bullet naming it would make the checker\'s A3e read your correct `:1077` removal as "a stays-line removed" (measured 22:06 on the real checker). Do NOT touch line 473; the second control cell reds if you do.\n\n## The exact change — ONE SMALL EDIT in `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/startup-migrations.ts`, one hunk with 3 lines of context each side\n\nE1 — line 1077 becomes (context: line 1076 is `         WHERE a.id > b.id AND a.content_hash = b.content_hash`; line 1078 is the `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... uq_pdr_hash_tenant ...` line). **There is NO blank line anywhere in this hunk.** Header `@@ -1074,7 +1074,7 @@`:\n\n```\n@@ -1074,7 +1074,7 @@\n         // UNIQUE index the verification.ts ON CONFLICT clause errors.\n         `DELETE FROM platform_document_registry a USING platform_document_registry b\n          WHERE a.id > b.id AND a.content_hash = b.content_hash\n-           AND COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\') = COALESCE(b.tenant_id, \'\')`,\n+           AND a.tenant_id IS NOT DISTINCT FROM b.tenant_id`,\n         `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS uq_pdr_hash_tenant ON platform_document_registry(content_hash, tenant_id)`,\n         `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS platform_document_type_templates (\n           id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),\n```\n\nThe `+` line is byte-exact — copy it: **11 leading spaces**, then `AND a.tenant_id IS NOT DISTINCT FROM b.tenant_id`, then the closing backtick and comma (`` `, ``) exactly as the `-` line had them. **Put NO comment on this line**: it sits INSIDE a SQL template string, so a `// KS-1272` there would be sent to Postgres as SQL and break the statement. Every context line is ONE space followed by the source line unchanged (the source lines are indented 8, 8, 9, 8, 8 and 10 spaces, so the context lines start with 9, 9, 10, 9, 9 and 11 spaces). The `+` line contains no non-ASCII character, no dollar sign and no double quote.\n\n## The test — CREATE THE NEW FILE `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1272-platform-dedup-uuid-tenant-id.test.ts`\n\n**Reference for the harness (READ-ONLY, do not modify, do not add it to your diff):** `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1062-startup-migrations-tenant-summary-first-error.test.ts` — this file copies its imports, `PRODUCT` / `SCRATCH` / `FAKE` / `EMPTY_MIGRATIONS_DIR` constants, `dbOf`, the `FakePool` class shape, `boot`, `metaOf`, the `beforeAll` redirect and the `afterAll` restore, and changes only the fake\'s rules, the summary finders and the cells. Write the 🔴 title with the literal 🔴 character, never as an escape sequence.\n\nWrite EXACTLY this file (85 lines). Two CONTROL cells first, then one 🔴 cell. Every line of it is given; do not add, drop or reorder anything. The apostrophe-free titles are deliberate — keep them.\n\n```\n/**\n * KS-1272 - the platform-DB de-dup DELETE in startup-migrations fails 22P02 on every boot where\n * platform_document_registry.tenant_id is uuid (docker/init-platform/01-platform-schema.sql declares it so):\n * the statement compares COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\'), and \'\' cannot be cast to uuid, so the gateway logs\n * "Migration FAILED on platform" and "Platform DB migrations INCOMPLETE - 1 FAILED" at every boot.\n * runStartupMigrations() is called DIRECTLY with pg redirected, ONLY for the product file, to the fake Pool\n * below (the ks1062 / ks1125 idiom); the fake behaves like a uuid-typed platform database: it refuses any\n * statement that coalesces tenant_id with \'\'. The controls prove the redirect, prove that ONE refused platform\n * statement is exactly what the platform summary counts, and pin that the MAIN list is not touched.\n */\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeAll, afterAll, vi } from \'vitest\';\nimport * as fs from \'fs\';\nimport * as os from \'os\';\nimport * as path from \'path\';\nimport Module from \'module\';\nconst PRODUCT = path.join(__dirname, \'..\', \'startup-migrations.ts\');\nconst SCRATCH = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \'ks1272-\'));\nconst FAKE = path.join(SCRATCH, \'fake-pg.cjs\');\nconst EMPTY_MIGRATIONS_DIR = path.join(SCRATCH, \'migrations\');\nconst PLATFORM_URL_BASE = \'postgresql://qauser:qapass@qa-platform.invalid:5432/\';\n/** What a uuid-typed tenant_id column refuses: the empty string cannot be cast to uuid. */\nconst UUID_COALESCE = "COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\')";\nconst UNIQUE_INDEX = \'CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS uq_pdr_hash_tenant\';\nlet lines: string[] = [];\nlet product: { runStartupMigrations: () => Promise<void>; CORE_MIGRATIONS: string[] };\nconst origResolve = (Module as any)._resolveFilename;\nfunction dbOf(connStr: string): string {\n  try { return new URL(connStr).pathname.replace(/^\\//, \'\'); } catch { return \'?\'; }\n}\n/** No I/O. qa_platform_uuid is a platform database whose tenant_id is uuid; qa_platform_index refuses one other statement. */\nclass FakePool {\n  private db: string;\n  constructor(opts: { connectionString: string }) { this.db = dbOf(opts.connectionString); }\n  async query(text: string): Promise<{ rows: unknown[]; rowCount: number }> {\n    if (this.db === \'qa_platform_uuid\' && String(text).includes(UUID_COALESCE)) throw new Error(\'invalid input syntax for type uuid: ""\');\n    if (this.db === \'qa_platform_index\' && String(text).includes(UNIQUE_INDEX)) throw new Error(\'qa planted refusal of the unique index\');\n    return { rows: [], rowCount: 0 };\n  }\n  async end(): Promise<void> { /* nothing to close */ }\n}\nasync function boot(platformDb: string): Promise<void> {\n  lines = [];\n  vi.stubEnv(\'PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL\', PLATFORM_URL_BASE + platformDb);\n  const spy = vi.spyOn(console, \'log\').mockImplementation((...a: unknown[]) => { lines.push(a.map(String).join(\' \')); });\n  try { await product.runStartupMigrations(); } finally { spy.mockRestore(); }\n}\nconst platformSummary = () => lines.find((l) => l.includes(\'[startup-migrations] Platform DB migrations\')) || \'\';\nconst mainSummary = () => lines.find((l) => l.includes(\'[startup-migrations] Main DB migrations\')) || \'\';\nconst metaOf = (line: string) => JSON.parse(line.replace(/^[^{]*/, \'\') || \'{}\');\nbeforeAll(async () => {\n  fs.mkdirSync(EMPTY_MIGRATIONS_DIR);\n  fs.writeFileSync(FAKE, \'module.exports = globalThis.__KS1272_FAKE_PG;\\n\');\n  (globalThis as any).__KS1272_FAKE_PG = { Pool: FakePool };\n  (Module as any)._resolveFilename = function (request: string, parent: any, ...rest: unknown[]) {\n    if (request === \'pg\' && parent && parent.filename === PRODUCT) return FAKE;\n    return origResolve.call(this, request, parent, ...rest);\n  };\n  vi.stubEnv(\'DATABASE_URL\', \'postgresql://qauser:qapass@qa-main.invalid:5432/qa_main\');\n  vi.stubEnv(\'MIGRATIONS_DIR\', EMPTY_MIGRATIONS_DIR);\n  delete process.env.MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL;\n  delete process.env.MIGRATION_PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL;\n  delete process.env.MULTI_TENANCY_ENABLED;\n  delete process.env.APP_DB_PASSWORD;\n  product = await import(\'../startup-migrations\');\n});\nafterAll(() => {\n  (Module as any)._resolveFilename = origResolve;\n  vi.unstubAllEnvs();\n  fs.rmSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true, force: true });\n});\ndescribe(\'KS-1272: the platform de-dup DELETE on a uuid-typed tenant_id\', () => {\n  it(\'control: pg resolves to the fake, and ONE refused platform statement (the unique index) is what the platform summary counts as 1 FAILED\', async () => {\n    expect(Module.createRequire(PRODUCT).resolve(\'pg\')).toBe(FAKE);\n    await boot(\'qa_platform_index\');\n    expect([platformSummary().startsWith(\'[WARN] [startup-migrations] Platform DB migrations INCOMPLETE \'), metaOf(platformSummary())]).toEqual([true, { applied: 6, failed: 1 }]);\n  });\n  it(\'control: the MAIN list keeps exactly one COALESCE de-dup on tenant_id (NULL and empty equal on its TEXT column) and the main summary is complete\', async () => {\n    await boot(\'qa_platform_index\');\n    expect([product.CORE_MIGRATIONS.filter((s) => s.includes(UUID_COALESCE)).length, mainSummary().startsWith(\'[INFO] [startup-migrations] Main DB migrations complete \'), metaOf(mainSummary()).failed]).toEqual([1, true, 0]);\n  });\n  it(\'🔴 KS-1272: on a platform database whose tenant_id is uuid, the de-dup DELETE is accepted and the platform summary is complete with 0 FAILED\', async () => {\n    await boot(\'qa_platform_uuid\');\n    expect([platformSummary().startsWith(\'[INFO] [startup-migrations] Platform DB migrations complete \'), metaOf(platformSummary())]).toEqual([true, { applied: 7, failed: 0 }]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## THE RED-FIRST CELL — state it to yourself before you write a line\n\n**At the UNTOUCHED tip, `🔴 KS-1272: on a platform database whose tenant_id is uuid, ...` FAILS, by assertion.** The platform list\'s DELETE at `:1075-:1077` contains `COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\')`; the fake for `qa_platform_uuid` throws `invalid input syntax for type uuid: ""` on it; `migrateDatabase` counts it (`:834-:841`, the message does not say "already exists"); the summary at `:1096-:1100` is `[WARN] [startup-migrations] Platform DB migrations INCOMPLETE — 1 FAILED {"applied":6,"failed":1}`; the cell reads `[false, { applied: 6, failed: 1 }]` against `[true, { applied: 7, failed: 0 }]`. After your one-line hunk the statement no longer coalesces `tenant_id` with `\'\'`, the fake accepts it, and the summary is `[INFO] [startup-migrations] Platform DB migrations complete {"applied":7,"failed":0}` — GREEN.\n\nThe two CONTROLS are GREEN on BOTH trees: `qa_platform_index` refuses only the unique-index statement, so the platform summary is `INCOMPLETE — 1 FAILED {applied: 6, failed: 1}` before and after (the instrument can see one refused platform statement); and the MAIN list still carries exactly ONE statement with `COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\')` (`:473`) while the main summary is `complete` with `failed: 0` — a diff that also edits `:473` reds this control (measured: `[0, true, 0]` against `[1, true, 0]`), and a diff that edits ONLY `:473` leaves the 🔴 cell red.\n\n**MEASURED, not predicted** (brief-writer 22:00-22:02 AEST 2026-09-20, in a `git clone --shared` of the checkout detached at `dc061f2bb`, farmed and shared-built by `tasks/code_patch/prepare_clone.sh` rc 0; the repo\'s own vitest 4.1.9): tip + this exact test → `1 failed / 3` (the 🔴 cell, `AssertionError: expected [ false, { applied: 6, failed: 1 } ] to deeply equal [ true, { applied: 7, failed: +0 } ]`), both controls green; tip + this exact hunk (`git apply --check` strict rc 0) + this test → `3 passed / 3`; whole api-gateway suite `674 passed / 674` at the tip and `677 / 677` with the patch; `tsc --noEmit -p .` rc 0 on both trees; the test file alone under the checker\'s own `--types node,vitest/globals` call → rc 0, 0 diagnostics (a planted `const ks1272Plant: number = "x"` in a copy gives rc 2, TS2322, so the check sees the file).\n\n## Red cells\n\n- 🔴 KS-1272: on a platform database whose tenant_id is uuid, the de-dup DELETE is accepted and the platform summary is complete with 0 FAILED\n\n## Output\n\nExactly ONE ```diff block, nothing outside it, containing TWO sections in this order:\n1. `--- a/Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/startup-migrations.ts` / `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/startup-migrations.ts`, ONE hunk `@@ -1074,7 +1074,7 @@` — 3 context lines, **1** `-` line (1077), **1** `+` line, 3 context lines. None of them empty.\n2. `--- /dev/null` / `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1272-platform-dedup-uuid-tenant-id.test.ts`, ONE hunk `@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@` whose new-count equals the number of lines you actually emit (85 if you copy the file exactly; count them), every line a `+`.\n\n## Premises (measured)\n\nAll times AEST 2026-09-20, each read from `date` in the run that produced it. Scratch = `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-DevMASTER-WEDNESDAY/3cf58e87-cbe7-4022-b8e2-5a8f58cc4e8b/scratchpad/ks1272/` (`K/`). `K/clone2` = `git clone --shared --no-checkout` of the Secuura checkout, `checkout --detach dc061f2bb`, farmed + shared-built by `tasks/code_patch/prepare_clone.sh` (rc 0, 21:59:30). Nothing was deleted; every write verb ran in the scratch clone(s), restored by `git checkout --` (clone porcelain 0 after every run).\n\n- **P1 tip.** `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/develop` on the Secuura checkout = `dc061f2bb6dff9180a0724b1d1d5c50b9a0173fa` (21:52:51); `cat-file -t` = commit (local, no override needed). `git log -1`: `dc061f2bb KS-1282 N99-1: pin that a tenant ADMIN JWT is refused 403 on GET /api/platform/tenants (#1101)`. Source checkout porcelain (tracked) 0 at 21:52:51 and after every run.\n- **P2 the file at the tip.** `startup-migrations.ts` blob `ed3e52142`, 1227 lines. `COALESCE(a.tenant_id` occurs exactly TWICE: `:473` (5-space indent, `CORE_MIGRATIONS`) and `:1077` (11-space indent, `platformMigrations`). `platformMigrations` (`:1060-:1093`) holds 7 statements: extension, table, 2 indexes, the DELETE, the unique index, the templates table — so one refused statement is `{applied: 6, failed: 1}`, the ticket\'s own kintsugi numbers. Lines `:1074-:1080` carry no blank line and no non-ASCII character. The `+` line: 0 non-ASCII, 0 dollar signs, 0 double quotes.\n- **P3 the reference at the tip.** `ks1062-...test.ts` blob `0ec64a16e`, 111 lines; api-gateway `package.json` `"test": "vitest"`, vitest `^4.1.9`, pg `^8.18.0`. Tests at the tip that import `startup-migrations`: ks1062, ks1125, ks667 (3 of 68 files); none names `COALESCE(a.tenant_id` or `Platform DB migrations` (0 hits each), so no existing cell pins either line.\n- **P4 red and green MEASURED** — see the red-first section (`K/measure.sh`, 22:00:47-22:01:20, outputs `K/m/out/`). Mis-scoped variants (`K/measure2.sh`, 22:02:07-22:02:08): edit `:473` ONLY → 2 failed / 3 (the 🔴 cell still red AND the main-list control red `[0, true, 0]`); edit BOTH `:473` and `:1077` → 1 failed / 3 (the main-list control red). Test-file-alone tsc rc 0 / 0 lines; planted control rc 2, 1 × TS2322.\n- **P5 this brief through the real checker** (`tasks/code_patch/checker.sh` sha256 `d824fa3a6930fc9e…`, outputs `K/ck/draft/` and `K/ck/placed/`; each model-shaped output assembled FROM this brief\'s fences by `K/assemble.py`): draft input built rc 0 (~24.0K prompt tokens; 5 sites, 1 must_change; 1 expected `+`; 1 red cell). Golden 22:07:07-22:07:33: **RESULT: PASS (7/7)** — A2 strict; A3 {product, the new test}; A3b 1/1; A3c 1/1 + A3d clean; A3i 1 line byte-exact incl. leading whitespace; A4 `1 failed / 3 run; controls green; assertion reds`; A5 3/3; A6 674 → 677, NEW reds `[]`; A7 rc 0; INFO test-file tsc rc 0. Wrong variants: `sqlcomment` (a `// KS-1272` INSIDE the SQL string on the `+` line) → **FAIL A3c INCOMPLETE 1 of 1**; `coalesce_text` (`COALESCE(a.tenant_id::text, \'\') = ...`, a plausible other fix) → **FAIL A3c INCOMPLETE 1 of 1**; `only473` (the hunk placed at `:470-:476`, 5-space indent) → **FAIL A3i INDENT SHIFT :473 indent 5, brief 11**; `both` (`:473` AND `:1077` edited, two hunks) → A4 PASS then **FAIL A5** (the main-list control red, `1 failed / 3`) and **FAIL A6** (1 NEW red, the same cell). Draft run 1 (with a `:473 (correct)` bullet in `## Where`): golden **FAIL A3e :473** at 22:06:33 — the bullet was removed, see the notes.\n\n## Notes for the raise (not for the model)\n\n- **Behaviour change:** on the PLATFORM database only, the KS-39 #4 de-dup DELETE compares `a.tenant_id IS NOT DISTINCT FROM b.tenant_id` instead of `COALESCE(a.tenant_id, \'\') = COALESCE(b.tenant_id, \'\')`. On a uuid column the statement now runs (it raised 22P02 before, so it never deleted anything there); on a TEXT platform column the ONLY difference is that a NULL and an \'\' tenant_id are no longer treated as duplicates of each other. The main database\'s `:473` is untouched, on purpose (see "NOT in this task").\n- **Raise tier: TIER 2. Refs KS-1272, not Closes** — the ticket\'s third bullet ("decide which declaration is canonical: init schema `UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES tenants(id)` vs the in-code `TEXT`") is a ruling, not briefed. The kintsugi log line itself is UNMEASURED by this brief (no box access from the drafter); the mechanism is reproduced by the fake exactly as the ticket reproduced it with `SELECT COALESCE(NULL::uuid, \'\')`.\n- **Why `:473` is not a `## Where` bullet:** the checker\'s A3e (a stays-site removed) matches by STRIPPED TEXT, and `:473` and `:1077` are identical stripped — with a `:473 (correct)` bullet the GOLDEN output FAILS `A3e ... :473` (measured 22:06:33, real checker, draft run 1). The guard for `:473` is the second control cell (A5) plus the prose.\n- **Why the `## Where` is NOT line-keyed:** `night/build_input.sh` takes a line-keyed site\'s quote as the FIRST single-backtick span of the bullet, and the tip\'s `:1077` itself ends with a backtick (`` `, `` closes the SQL template string), so no single-backtick quote can equal it — a line-keyed copy of this Where IS refused at build: `REFUSED KS-1272 — line-keyed ## Where: :1075 — the brief quotes \'\' but the tip\'s line 1075 is ...` (measured 22:05, `NIGHT_BRIEFS_DIR` pointed at a scratch copy whose heading carried the word; the first bullet whose line starts with a backti